Wearing metal armor is a good strategy in the early game. It improves
your likelyhood of surviving.

>Upon starting the game, I immediately quaff any b !oEH for HP.

Personally I would delay. There are usually between 4 and 8 max HP that
can be blessed on you from your god if you simply use a bit of strategy
and patience. You god will add max HP for you if you are currently below
5HP, have less than 16 max HP @ XL1 or 21 @ XL2, and can pray. It's
considered major trouble and will always be granted.

So when I know I can pray (which is at turn 300) I stand next to a newt
or jackal and let them peck away until I get under 5HP, then pray. Often
I can go a couple of rounds at XL1 and then get another round at XL2
sometimes if I'm still below 21 HP by the time I get to XL2. Then and
only then will I quaff the blessed !oEH.

