It's SOP for me. I'm not in any hurry about it though. Usually I'll
wander the dungeon up to DL5 or so, buffing the pet and cleaning out any
shops I come across. I also will BUC test and put on any armor I happen
across too. Getting an non cursed hard helment is essential for dealing
with falling rock traps in the mines.

With a healer it's pretty simple to maintain oneself and the pet during
this phase. You know exactly how many HP the critter has and can cast
healing when they get low. Also healer money makes it for efficient for
cleaning out shops since you're already starting with a good initial
stash. Personally I credit clone, but even having the pet steal and
redrop items wouldn't take too terribly long.

>Once I
>obtain decent armor (yes, I wear metal armor on a healer),

All spellcasters need to wear metal armor in the early game. Lowering
one's AC is essential for survival. Eventually you'll get enchanted
armor and dragon scale, which provides lower AC without the spellcasting
penalty. Also I specifically run tthe protection racket to get the
opportunity to trade heavy metal, spellkilling armor for divine
protection.

